    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3102" root="بل" body-key="b">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابلّ</span></b>  <i>It</i> (wood, or a branch or twig,) <i>had the
sap,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَآء</span>, K,) or <i>the produce of the rain,</i> (O,)
<i>flowing in it.</i> (O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلَّ</span>, in four
places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>He</i> (a man) <i>resisted,</i> or <i>withstood, and
overcame.</i> (As, T, S. [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبَلَ</span>.]) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابلّ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَيْهِ</span> <i>He overcame him.</i> (M, K.) [See an ex. in
a verse of Sá'ideh, cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَسْفٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He
wearied by badness,</i> or <i>wickedness:</i> (M, K:) or
<i>he wearied another in aiding him to accomplish
his desire.</i> (TA. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبِلٌّ</span>.]) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3- <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْلَلْتُهُ</span> <i>I made
him to go away.</i> (Msb.)

